    "chunk_size_bytes": 1958,
    "chunk_text": "IV ^wd& jeks fldgi \u2013 YS% ,xld m%cd;dka;s%l iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h - 2019'06'24Part IV (B) \u2013 GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA \u2013 24.06.20191A\n\nw;s \u00fafYI\n\nwxl 2129$3 - 2019 cqks ui 24 jeks i\u00f7od - 2019'06'24No. 2129/3 - MONDAY JUNE 24, 2019\n\nEXTRAORDINARYThe Gazette of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka\n\nFILLING OF A VACANCY IN THE OFFICE OF CHAIRMAN OF THE EMBILIPITIYAPRADESHIYA SABHA UNDER SECTION 66B(2) OF THE LOCAL AUTHORITIES ELECTIONSORDINANCE (CHAPTER 262) AS AMENDED BY LOCAL AUTHORITIES ELECTION (AMENDED)ACT, NO. 16 OF 2017\n\nWHEREAS the office of Chairman in Embilipitiya Pradeshiya Sabha has fallen vacant by reason of loss of seat or office;\n\nAND WHEREAS the Secretary of the Sri Lanka Podujana Peramuna, the recognized political party to whichMeegasdeniya Kankanamge Amil the Former Chairman belonged, was required by me under Section 66B(2) of the aforesaidordinance, to decide upon the member of Embilitpitiya Pradeshiya Sabha who belongs to such party who shall bedeclared elected as chairman within a period of thirty (30) days ;\n\nAND WHEREAS the Secretary of the aforesaid recognized political party has communicated his decision tonominate Weerasinghage Surantha Jayalath to fill such vacancy ;\n\nNOW THEREFORE, I, Suranga Ambagahathenne, Returning Officer of the Embilipitiya Pradeshiya Sabha, actingin terms of Section 66B(2) of the Local Authorities Elections Ordinance (Chapter 262) as amended by Local AuthoritiesElection (amended) Act, No. 16 of 2017 do hereby declare Weerasinghage Surantha Jayalath elected as chairman of theEmbilipitiya Pradeshiya Sabha.\n\nSURANGA AMBAGAHATHENNE,Returning Officer,Embilipitiya Pradeshiya Sabha.District Election Office,Ratnapura,20th June, 2019.\n\n07 - 194/1\n\nY%S ,xld m%cd;dka;%sl iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha .ei\u00dc m;%h\n\n(Published by Authority)\n\nPART IV (B) \u2014 LOCAL GOVERNMENT\n\nNotices under the Local Authorities Elections Ordinance"
  },
